  m_Name: DiskBrakeEngineData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Disk Brake Engine
  engineDescription: 'A disc brake is a mechanical braking system that slows or stops
    a rotating wheel by applying friction between brake pads and a rotating disc
    (rotor). From an engineering perspective, its performance depends on efficient
    heat dissipation, friction characteristics, structural strength, and material
    selection. The rotor is typically made of cast iron or steel to withstand high
    thermal and mechanical loads, while brake pads use friction materials designed
    for consistent braking and wear resistance. Key design considerations include
    braking torque, thermal expansion, cooling efficiency, durability, vibration
    control, and manufacturing accuracy. Proper disc brake design ensures reliable
    stopping performance, safety, reduced wear, and long service life under varying
    operating conditions.

'
